; A silent frame keeps the filter of the frame before it. Per frame in: snd (INP at frm) and K10..K1 (INP at gx);
; out, the frame's Ks (OUT at wa): its own if it sounds (snd 1), else the ones before again. The Ks before go round
; on this machine's own pile (OUT at pz and wb back to INP at go), ten zeros before the first frame. The two OUTs
; are set each frame: OUT x (the new Ks) or OUT o (the old).
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            start   CLA   n9       03-10: ten zeros on the pile
  04                    STO   i
  05            pz      OUT   z
  06                    CLA   i
  07                    SUB   00
  08                    STO   i
  09                    TAC   frm
  10                    JMP   pz
  11            frm     INP   snd      11-23: a frame: new Ks or old
  12                    CLA   wox
  13                    STO   w
  14                    CLA   snd
  15                    SUB   00
  16                    TAC   old
  17                    SUB   00
  18                    TAC   set
  19            old     CLA   woo
  20                    STO   w
  21            set     CLA   w
  22                    STO   wa
  23                    STO   wb
  24                    CLA   n9       24-34: the ten Ks
  25                    STO   i
  26            gx      INP   x
  27            go      INP   o
  28            wa      DATA  0        (OUT x or OUT o)
  29            wb      DATA  0        (OUT x or OUT o)
  30                    CLA   i
  31                    SUB   00
  32                    STO   i
  33                    TAC   frm
  34                    JMP   gx
  40            snd     DATA  0
  41            x       DATA  0
  42            o       DATA  0
  43            w       DATA  0
  44            i       DATA  0
  45            z       DATA  0
  46            n9      DATA  9
  47            wox     OUT   x
  48            woo     OUT   o
